You are reviewing, not building. Do not edit any file in the repo; scratch probe scripts under /tmp are fine.

Review the M5 (vision), M5U (upload mode) and M5O (Spark Open via Baseten, second opinion, fallback, engine-sound DSP)
work: `git diff b9b1a9a -- backend packages android scripts` plus any uncommitted changes (`git status`). Check against AGENTS.md hard constraints and docs/SPEC.md §5 and §7:
- correctness bugs (wrong math, wrong units, off-by-one, unhandled error paths, races in the async routes);
- constraint violations: an LLM output that can move a posterior or set a probability, a non-Meta call, a contributor
  model ID, secrets or request headers reaching fixtures/events/logs, in-place mutation of session history,
  safety gates that are prompt text instead of code;
- replay determinism: anything that makes a cached replay differ or spend money;
- budget guard holes: any paid call path that skips the hard stop or logs a cost of 0;
- tests that pass without checking the real behaviour.
Run commands in the foreground only (no background shells or subagents); you may run single test files but
the full suite is already green. Give the review as your final answer (it is saved for you): findings ranked most severe first, each with file:line, the concrete failure
scenario, and the fix. Only real findings you verified by reading the code; no style nits. End with a one-line verdict.
